  "notes": "Mask-constrained Kontext replacement with IP-Adapter identity conditioning (v0.3.0). The BASE image (current room state) feeds VAEEncodeForInpaint whose noise mask confines sampling to the affected region - unmasked pixels keep the base exactly. The REFERENCE stays conditioning-only (ReferenceLatent path, retained as a locality hint) so a whole-room reference can no longer collapse the output onto itself; identity transfer is now carried by the XLabs IPAdapterFlux path: node 25 loads the CROPPED reference (control_image role, same asset as reference_image), node 23 loads the CLIP-Vision encoder, node 24 loads the FLUX IP-Adapter weights, and node 27 patches the UNET before KSampler 13. The mask PNG (white=edit region, linear feather ramp baked in server-side) binds through ImageToMask(red). VERIFY-PHASE1b: IPAdapterFlux/IPAdapterModelLoader/CLIPVisionLoader input names and the need for node 24 are BEST-GUESS (XLabs ComfyUI-IPAdapter-Flux) and must be confirmed against the box fork object_info before deploy; node inputs verified against the box fork object_info (v9.1): ImageToMask(image,channel), VAEEncodeForInpaint(pixels,vae,mask,grow_mask_by 0..64), ConditioningSetMask(conditioning,mask,strength,set_cond_area); FeatherMask node deliberately not used (no single feather input - feathering is baked into the mask PNG server-side)."
